1
00:04:41,739 --> 00:04:47,739
If war is Hell, then what comes after?

2
00:09:23,478 --> 00:09:29,478
The Good German is a drama, mystery, romance film directed by Steven Soderbergh.

3
00:14:05,217 --> 00:14:11,217
An American journalist arrives in Berlin just after the end of World War Two.

4
00:18:46,956 --> 00:18:52,956
He becomes involved in a murder mystery surrounding a dead GI who washes up at a
lakeside mansion during the Potsdam negotiations between the Allied powers.

5
00:23:28,695 --> 00:23:34,695
Soon his investigation connects with his search for
his married pre-war German lover.

6
00:28:10,434 --> 00:28:16,434
Jake Geismar, played by George Clooney.

7
00:32:52,173 --> 00:32:58,173
Lena Brandt, played by Cate Blanchett.

8
00:37:33,913 --> 00:37:39,913
Tully, played by Tobey Maguire.

9
00:42:15,652 --> 00:42:21,652
Colonel Muller, played by Beau Bridges.

10
00:46:57,391 --> 00:47:03,391
Danny, played by Tony Curran.

11
00:51:39,130 --> 00:51:45,130
Bernie Teitel, played by Leland Orser.

12
00:56:20,869 --> 00:56:26,869
The Good German is a 2006 American neo-noir crime film.

13
01:01:02,608 --> 01:01:08,608
A film adaptation of Joseph Kanon's  2001 novel, it was directed by Steven
Soderbergh, and stars George Clooney, Cate Blanchett, and Tobey Maguire.

14
01:05:44,347 --> 01:05:50,347
Set in Berlin following the Allied victory over the Nazis, it begins as a murder mystery but weaves in
elements involving the American postwar employment of Nazi rocket scientists in Operation Paperclip.

15
01:10:26,086 --> 01:10:32,086
The film was shot in black-and-white and is designed to imitate the appearance of film noir from the 1940s, although it also
includes material – such as sex scenes and swearing – that would have been prohibited by the Production Code.

16
01:15:07,826 --> 01:15:13,826
Its poster is a homage to the poster for Casablanca (1942, also from
Warner Bros.), as is the closing scene at an airport.

17
01:19:49,565 --> 01:19:55,565
Besides being shot in black-and-white, the film was also shot in the traditional 1.37:1
aspect ratio (known as the Academy ratio), which declined in use from about 1953.

18
01:24:31,304 --> 01:24:37,304
The DVD release keeps the original aspect ratio, though the theatrical release, and other
DVD Releases, used the slightly more modern but still unusual 1.66:1 ratio.

19
01:29:13,043 --> 01:29:19,043
The film received mixed reviews and grossed $6 million
worldwide against a budget of $32 million.

20
01:33:54,782 --> 01:34:00,782
It was nominated for the Berlin International Film Festival Golden
Bear and the Academy Award for Best Original Score.

21
01:38:36,521 --> 01:38:42,521
The film explores themes of berlin, germany, chauffeur,
corruption, love of one's life, nazi.

22
01:43:18,260 --> 01:43:24,260
The tone is intense and emotional and mind_bending.
